#!/bin/zsh
# 台灣風 boss 三案的模擬圖（只是概念，定案後才照 jobs 格式生逐格動作）
cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.."
COM="HD-2D fantasy JRPG battle concept art in crisp pixel art, the same pixel art style, outline weight and cel shading as the reference image. The reference shows existing enemies of this game; redraw them as Taiwanese-fantasy versions that are still clearly recognizable (same face, hair, body shape, signature props) but with new costume details. Composition: a wide 16:9 battle scene, the enemy party stands on the LEFT two thirds of the image, all facing toward the RIGHT side in three-quarter view (body and face point the same way), the boss is the largest figure at the back, about twice as tall as the minions, minions stand in front of him in a loose row, full bodies visible, nothing cut off by the image edge. The right third of the image is empty floor where the heroes would stand. Rich atmospheric lighting but readable silhouettes. No text, no letters, no Chinese characters, no numbers, no logos, no user interface. No real deities, no real brands."
p1="$COM Scene: a corporate courtyard turned into a Taiwanese temple-fair plaza at night, cut-and-paste porcelain (jian nian) roof ridges with dragons, red palace lanterns, scattered firecracker paper, office tower windows still lit in the background. BOSS (redesign of the stout middle-aged manager in the reference): the Blame-Shifting Section Chief as a heavy armored general made of Taiwanese koji pottery and cut porcelain: broad shoulders, round belly, dark red suit under a peacock-blue battle robe, shoulder armor made of glazed porcelain shards in bright colors, two lantern-shaped banners on his back (blank, no writing), a huge black iron wok held as a shield, a long red-ink brush spear, suit trousers and pointed leather shoes still visible. Colors dark red, teal green, porcelain white, old gold. MINIONS: (1) the office drone foot soldier now wearing short lantern-patterned lamellar armor over his shirt, a red-tasseled brush spear instead of a pen, a wooden staff tag at his belt; (2) the filing-cabinet knight with teal glazed porcelain shards inlaid on the drawer armor and temple roof-ridge ornaments on the cabinet shield, a ceramic stamp hammer; (3) the know-nothing auntie with her curly perm, glasses, sleeve covers and ledger, now in a long lantern-pattern vest, ribbons on her feather duster, an embroidered cover on her thermos; (4) the parrot-headed officer with lantern tassels and porcelain epaulettes on his coat, a long red paper trailing from his quill."
p2="$COM Scene: a Taiwanese night market under an elevated highway stretching into darkness, layers of floating neon signboards (blank shapes, no writing), food stall carts with warm bulbs, steam and smoke. BOSS: the Night Market Operations Director, a tall thin manager in a purple-black suit wearing a cape made of neon signboards, standing on a floating food-stall cart throne, a pointed crown made of stacked blank price boards, many coin pouches and tokens on his chest, a giant change tray used as a shield and a calculator staff strung with copper coins, his face hidden in the backlight of the signs with glowing eyes. Colors electric purple, hot pink, cyan, oily black iron and warm yellow bulbs. MINIONS: (1) the office drone foot soldier wearing a night-market vendor apron over his shirt and a towel around his neck, holding tongs; (2) the deadline courier with feather cap, alarm clock and satchel, now in a reflective short cape with a long trailing queue-number paper scroll, cyan wind at his sneakers; (3) the energy-drink intern in the oversized suit, the green bottle crate now wrapped in an iron ice-bucket frame with green magic steam; (4) the pig-headed general in a gold-thread suit with a glowing champion light-board sash, his trophy hammer overflowing with tokens."
p3="$COM Scene: a rooftop sheet-metal add-on office in a typhoon, pouring rain, water tanks and air-conditioner units floating in the wind, a city of tilted signboards below, cold fluorescent light leaking from the windows. BOSS: the Illegal Rooftop Extension Director, a short stout administrator in a wrinkled suit and yellow raincoat sitting inside a huge walking exoskeleton built like a three-storey rooftop add-on: corrugated metal sheets, a water tank, AC brackets and rusty steel beams, an aluminium office window on its chest glowing with fluorescent light, a rolling steel shutter as a giant shield on the left arm, a steel-beam hammer with a meeting microphone tied on the right arm, his necktie blown horizontal by the wind, a fake video-call smile. Colors rust red, iron grey, raincoat yellow, cold white light. MINIONS: (1) the filing-cabinet knight with rusty red corrugated shoulder plates and a tarp tied on his cabinet shield, yellow tape on his stamp hammer; (2) the smelly old uncle with cane, slippers with socks and crooked cigarette, now in a torn raincoat, a small windsock on his cane, his grey smoke swirling in the rain; (3) the energy-drink intern in a clear plastic raincoat over the oversized suit, a waterproof cover on the green bottle crate; (4) the deadline courier with his feather cap tied down by a string, iron frame on the alarm clock, short cape blown into sharp wings."
run() { [ -s "design/taiwan/$1.png" ] || zsh tools/gen.sh "design/taiwan/$1.png" "$2" "design/taiwan/$3.png"; }
case $1 in 1) run mock_1 "$p1" ref1;; 2) run mock_2 "$p2" ref2;; 3) run mock_3 "$p3" ref3;; esac
